FIX FE VALUE-CYCLE SIGNATURE (785): F1/F2 track/car/mode cycle traps on wasm

The front-end value-cycle dispatch (**(code**)(&DAT_004697d4+uVar4*0x14))(local_1c)
types the call_indirect as (i32)->i32 (`code`=int() called with one arg). Its
four targets -- Toggle_Track, Toggle_Car, FUN_004509d8 (mode cycle), Null_Routine
(screens 3-7 filler) -- were void(int)/void(void), so wasm's call_indirect trapped
("null function or function signature mismatch") the moment F1/F2 was pressed. In
the native build the mismatch is ignored (cdecl), so the value-cycle worked there
and only the browser/wasm target was broken -- the exact browser-only track-select
gap. Widened all four to int(int); bare `return;` yields an unused i32 (callers
drop it). Signature-normalization class (patches 610/765).

